WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.367
-Welcome back. They love you.
-Wow! [ Laughs ]

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.534
-Come on!
-I'm, like, blushing.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.868
-I know! Come on.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.133
Welcome back to the show.
Thanks for coming on.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.133
I appreciate this.
We have so much to talk about.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.133
First of all, congratulations.
You're married.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.133
-I am, yes.
-This is fantastic!

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.834
How does it feel?
I met your husband.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.667
-Yeah, you did! You met Bader.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.200
-I met him backstage.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.534
How does it feel?
Are you...?

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.033
-It's great.
I mean, it's amazing.

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:25.367
I met my person.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.033
You never know if you're gonna
find that in life,

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:30.033
and he's an amazing guy, man,
and I love him,

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.534
and we're a great team.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.200
-I'm so happy for you.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.367
How long have you been married?

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.701
-We've been married since April.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.200
-Yeah.
-April 3rd.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.567
-I love it. Does it give you
a whole new perspective on life?

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.567
And you go, "Oh, yeah," you have
a buddy now that you can...

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.067
-You just get to share
everything with someone.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.467
And it's so special.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.634
Everything becomes that much
more important, I feel like.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:47.968
-I always wanted to tell you,
by the way,

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.300
I listened to your podcast.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.634
-Yeah.
-"The Lohdown."

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.234
And you're very good.
I mean, are you...

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.901
Usually, you're on the other
side getting interviewed.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.234
But do you like
interviewing people?

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.567
-I was so nervous when I did
my first interview.

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.801
Because I'm used to getting
the questions asked to me.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:01.968
I'm not used to asking
the questions.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:02.968
-But you're good at it.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.100
-Well, I got good at it.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.467
[ Both laugh ]
-Oh, the first...

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:06.934
I can't even watch the first --
-I was, like, sweating

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.133
the first one.
You can't see that

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.300
on the podcast, but...
-Oh, I can't watch

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.968
my first "Late Night."
I can't even look at it.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.367
I'm like...
-I think I was here for that.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:13.701
-I think you were here
the first week.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.033
Thank you for doing that.
I was stuttering.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.367
I was flop-sweating.
It was rough. It was rough.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:18.501
-And now look.
-Well, congrats.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:19.667
Yeah, now look. Yeah.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.667
Can we talk about
"Falling for Christmas"?

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.334
-Yeah.
-It's on Netflix.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.000
This is my type of movie,
by the way.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.501
I told you backstage,
I'm so into these movies,

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:28.734
these holiday movies.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.334
I want "Love, Actually"
every day of the year.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.000
Yeah, that's what I want.
-That's my Christmas choice too.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
-That's what I want
all the time.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.334
But let's -- can we set up
what this one's about?

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.501
-So, it's a girl
who kind of is an heiress

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:42.167
that has pretty much everything

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.767
and something happens to her,

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.267
she gets in a bad accident

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:46.934
and she gets amnesia

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:47.934
and remembers nothing.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.100
-Yep.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.367
-And I think
it's a beautiful story

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:53.267
because it's about how we always
want more things in life

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.767
but the simple things really
mean the most to us in the end.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.434
And that really --
I connected with that.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.601
I love that.
-It's gonna crush.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.501
I'm so happy.
-And it's really funny.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.834
I do a lot of physical comedy
in it, which was fun for me.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.667
-Yeah, and you sing in it,
by the way.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.000
-I do, yeah.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.501
-Can we talk about this?
'Cause -- no!

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
We love your voice.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:10.868
We want more singing.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:14.934
But the song of choice
is "Jingle Bell Rock."

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.534
Now, let me...

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.868
Let me remind
anyone who doesn't know,

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.200
but the last time you sang
"Jingle Bell Rock" in a movie

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.868
was in...
[ Audience cheers ]

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.534
..."Mean Girls.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:29.701
[ Cheering continues ]

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.367
How --
-Thank you!

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.868
How did it come about?

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.200
Whose idea was it to do
"Jingle Bell Rock"?

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.868
-Well, it was a joke, actually.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.868
I was kidding around
with the producers

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.701
and the director,
and I was like,

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:42.367
"Oh, it would be great
to do, you know, like,

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.734
a 'Jingle Bell Rock' skit."

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.400
And I -- I shouldn't
have said it,

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.901
because they went straight to,
"Oh, let's re-create

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.567
the 'Mean Girls'
talent show scene."

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.467
I was like, "Oh, no, no.
You can't touch 'Mean Girls.'"

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:53.801
Sorry, that's like...
You can't do that.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.100
[ Laughs ]

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.801
So then they were like,
"Oh, can you do the song?"

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.968
And so I was like,
gotta do the song.

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:00.367
-Yeah, you got to give them
what they want.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.701
Why not?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.200
-Everyone's loving it.
-I hope everyone likes it.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.200
-Ah, it's perfect
for the holidays.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.534
There was also --
I saw recently,

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.868
Jamie Lee Curtis was being
interviewed and they said,

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:14.200
"Would you ever want to do
a 'Freaky Friday' sequel?'

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.234
or something, and she said,
"I have a great idea for it

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:17.767
and I talked to" --
I think she said

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.100
she talked to you
or pitched you an idea.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.601
-We did speak about it, yeah.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:23.100
-And is there any truth to --
is it moving forward?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.267
Or is anyone --
-First of all,

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.100
let's just take the fact
that I was on set

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.434
filming at the time,

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.934
and Jamie Lee Curtis writes you,
and you just get excited

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.434
and distracted immediately.
-Of course.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.267
-So, I had to bring myself
down to earth and be like,

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.434
"Okay, I'm on set,
I have to focus."

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:36.934
And then she said
"Freaky Friday 2,"

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.601
and I got more excited.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.934
-Yeah, but then also the fans
were like, "Wait, this is good."

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:43.434
And the idea for the plot
was good, too.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:45.434
-[ Laughing ] Yeah, it is.
-Which, so -- yeah.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.100
But I mean, is there anyone --

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.434
-We would both be into it.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:49.767
-You would?
-Yeah.

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.267
-Let's get on this.
-I'm not gonna say no to Disney.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:55.267
-Let's make this into a thing.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.934
[ Applause ]

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.767
Any "Mean Girls 2"?

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:01.000
-I think that's
in Tina Fey's hands.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.000
-Okay, okay.
-And Lorne Michaels.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.834
-Tina, I know you're watching.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:07.167
Yeah, let's make that happen,
as well.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.334
I want to show everyone a clip,
though, of your new movie

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:10.834
right now,
"Falling for Christmas."

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.167
Take a look at this.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.000
-We just ran out
of pumpkin pancakes,

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.667
but if you'd like,
I can make you some eggs.

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:18.434
-Oh, please.
I'm perfectly capable

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:19.801
of making my own breakfast.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:23.133
♪♪

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:25.467
It's broken.
-Yeah, no, you just gotta...

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.067
You gotta push it in
and then twist it.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.734
-Thank you.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.167
Oh! This comes out fast.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.934
-Egg?
-Thank you.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.234
-Oh!

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.100
Well, you showed that egg
who's boss.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.767
-[ Chuckles ] A little messy.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.267
-You know what? Um...
Why don't you sit over there,

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:50.100
and I will take care of...
all of this.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.601
-Okay. Good idea.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ohh!

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:55.133
I love Olivia.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.968
-Olivia Perez.
-Olivia Perez. I love her!

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:58.801
What a great actress.
So cute.

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:00.200
Lindsay Lohan, everybody!

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:05.367
"Falling for Christmas"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:07.033
Lindsay and I are doing
something fun

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.634
after the break.
Stick around, everybody.

